<Legal t={en} title="Security and vulnerability reports" updated="2026-11-27">
  <h2>How VanKey protects your data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The vault is encrypted with XChaCha20-Poly1305, and its key is derived from your password with Argon2id. The recovery key is derived with HKDF-SHA256.</li>
    <li>Your password never leaves the device. The server sees only the derived login key, and hashes it again before storing.</li>
    <li>The server keeps only encrypted vaults and hashes of tokens. Refresh tokens rotate, and if an old token is reused after a short grace period, that device is removed.</li>
    <li>Repeated failed sign-ins are temporarily locked, per IP address and per account.</li>
    <li>The app slows down repeated wrong unlock attempts, hides 2FA codes and passwords after a while, and keeps secrets out of the Windows clipboard history.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is not done yet</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The encryption has not been reviewed by an independent auditor.</li>
    <li>Fingerprint and Windows Hello unlock have not been tested on every kind of device. Anyone whose fingerprint is enrolled on the device can still open the app.</li>
    <li>If you leave the vault open and lose the device, whoever holds it can read the data. Turn on auto-lock.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reporting a vulnerability</h2>
  <p>Please report privately rather than publicly before a fix is available:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use GitHub's private reporting: the repository page, <strong>Security → Report a vulnerability</strong>.</li>
    <li>Or email <a href="mailto:vankey@onigix.com">vankey@onigix.com</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Reports should include the steps to reproduce, the app version and the impact observed. Testing must not access data or accounts that do not belong to the tester. Expected response time: 3 working days.</p>
</Legal>
